      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When crafting a formal declaration to an embassy, it's essential to be precise, respectful, and concise. Start your communication with proper salutations, clearly state your claim, and provide the necessary legal documents to support your assertion. Here's a basic structure in English:\n\n---\n\n[Your Full Name]\n[Your Contact Information]\n[Address]\n[City, State, Zip Code]\n[Email Address]\n[Date]\n\nEmbassy of [Country Name]\n[Territory of [Country Name]]\nLeipziger Straße 6\nD-10117 Berlin, Germany\n\n[Embassy's Name]\n[Recipient's Full Name, Title]\nAmbassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary\n\nSubject: Declaration of Intent and Claim to the Valerius Estate\n\nDear Ambassador [Name],\n\nI am writing to formally declare my claim to the Valerius estate and to present my status as the last direct descendant of the principality in question. I have recently uncovered substantial family records that refute the long-held belief that the claim had been extinguished in 1922. Deeming it my duty to preserve our family's legacy and rightful inheritance, I hereby submit these documents as evidence to support my claim.\n\nEnclosed, please find the following documents with my declaration:\n1.",
